# PK:
# Tape Saturation — Studer/Ampex-inspired tape-machine coloration channel.
# A clean op-amp input/drive stage pushes a VOLTAGE-DRIVEN Jiles-Atherton tape
# head (the magnetic "tape" element). The head adds drive-dependent harmonic
# colour; a playback EQ + makeup stage follow. Drive sets how hard the head and
# electronics run, so tape saturation TRACKS the Drive control at line level.
# Type: tape saturation (outboard studio gear)
#
# PROVENANCE
#   Tape magnetics — Jiles-Atherton hysteresis model:
#     D.C. Jiles & D.L. Atherton, "Theory of ferromagnetic hysteresis",
#     J. Magn. Magn. Mater. 61 (1986) 48-60. Wave-digital tape realization
#     after J. Chowdhury, "Real-time physical modelling for analog tape
#     machines" (DAFx-19, 2019) and the CHOW Tape Model.
#   Voltage-driven head — a record/playback head is a tiny gap/coil whose
#     magnetic field is driven by the head GAP VOLTAGE (H ∝ V), so it reaches
#     its J-A knee at line level — unlike an output-transformer core (driven by
#     Ampere-law magnetizing CURRENT) whose knee needs hundreds of mA.
#   Head bump + HF loss — the low-frequency "head bump" and treble loss of a
#     tape machine are deliberate, loved parts of the sound. See Sound on Sound
#     "Analogue Warmth"/"Tape Saturation" and Studer/Accutronics literature.
#
# SIGNAL FLOW
#   in -> C_in -> [U0 buffer] -> [U1 Drive amp]
#      -> C_drv -> R_pri -> TH_tape (voltage-driven J-A head, series) -> R_sec
#      -> [playback EQ: head-bump LF shelf + HF rolloff/Tone]
#      -> [U2 makeup amp] -> Output level pot -> out
#
# CONTROLS
#   Drive  — how hard the head and electronics are pushed (level + saturation)
#   Tone   — playback HF tilt (CCW darker, CW brighter) — see note 4
#   Output — makeup / output level
#
# UNITS / FLAGS
#   [V] supplies +/-15 V — studio line-level op-amp rails (tape electronics
#       live well above the 9 V guitar-pedal rail).
#   [V] the tape head colours on gap VOLTAGE (H = kv*V); the Drive stage swings
#       the head voltage toward its ~1 V J-A knee, so saturation tracks Drive.
#
# NOTES (audit — measured, see tests/tape_saturation.rs):
#   1. SATURATION TRACKS DRIVE (the key feature). The voltage-driven tape_head
#      reaches its J-A knee at line level, so THD climbs monotonically with
#      Drive — measured ~0.0006 (Drive 0) to ~0.06 (Drive 1) at 120 Hz, in=0.05.
#      The studio head model (in compiler/components/tape_head.rs ::studio_head):
#      Ms=3.5e5 A/m, a=1500, alpha=1.6e-3, k=30, c=0.65, kv=8000 A/m/V,
#      Isat=200 uA, Gp=80 uS, h_bias=400 A/m, Rp=1 kΩ. (kv places the knee at
#      ~1 V; a/k/c widen the clean region; h_bias adds asymmetry — see note 3.)
#   2. REFERENCE LEVEL IS SANE & LEVEL-INDEPENDENT at small signal. With R_in
#      setting the drive gain and the makeup amp (R_o1/R_o2) trimming back, the
#      500 Hz reference gain at Drive=0.35 sits near unity (~+1 dB, spread
#      < 0.5 dB across in=0.02..0.1) — see flat-level sanity test.
#   3. HARMONIC CHARACTER IS PREDOMINANTLY ODD at working drive. The voltage
#      head is a symmetric saturator; its h_bias record-asymmetry (even-rich
#      colour) survives only at very low drive and is washed out by the
#      AC-coupled WDF stage extraction at hot levels. Restoring drive-tracking
#      EVEN harmonics needs an asymmetric clip/bias path that does not cancel
#      through the stage extraction — future refinement.
#   4. PLAYBACK EQ IS FLAT in v1. The head is resistive (no integrator), and
#      the post-stage R_bump/C_bump/R_hf/C_hf/Tone playback EQ still does not
#      propagate through the current WDF lowering (downstream-passive limit, see
#      the ignored Tone-authority test). Passband is flat (< 1 dB ripple
#      50 Hz-8 kHz, measured). An active, lowering-propagated playback EQ is the
#      future refinement that restores the head-bump + HF-loss voicing.
#   5. NO BIAS OSCILLATOR, NO WOW/FLUTTER, NO PRINT-THROUGH in v1. AC bias
#      linearization, transport wow/flutter and inter-layer print-through are
#      not modelled. (The delay_line(medium: tape_oxide) element models HF
#      self-demagnetization for a separate echo use-case.)

equipment "Tape Saturation" {
  supplies {
    V+: 15V
    V-: -15V
  }
  components {
    # === Input buffer ===
    C_in: cap(1u)            # input DC block
    R1:   resistor(1M)       # input reference to ground
    U0:   opamp(tl072)       # high-Z input buffer

    # === Drive stage (inverting amp, Drive = series feedback pot) ===
    R_in: resistor(1k)       # inverting input resistor (sets drive headroom)
    U1:   opamp(ne5532)      # low-noise drive amp (50 ohm out, drives iron)
    R_fb: resistor(10k)      # minimum feedback resistor
    Drive: pot(100k, a)      # gain = (R_fb + Drive)/R_in (audio taper)

    # === Magnetic colour: voltage-driven J-A tape head ===
    C_drv:  cap(47u)         # couple drive amp into the head
    TH_tape: tape_head()     # <-- THE VOLTAGE-DRIVEN J-A TAPE HEAD (saturates with Drive)
    R_pri:  resistor(470)    # head build-out / drive source impedance
    R_sec:  resistor(2.2k)   # head load (sets passband gain + tilt)

    # === Playback EQ: head-bump LF shelf ===
    R_bump: resistor(2.2k)   # head-bump shelf series resistor
    C_bump: cap(2.2u)        # bypasses R_bump at LF -> low-frequency lift

    # === Playback EQ: HF rolloff + Tone ===
    R_hf:   resistor(3.3k)   # HF tilt series resistor
    C_hf:   cap(2.2n)        # HF shunt cap (tape treble loss)
    Tone:   pot(100k)        # playback HF tilt

    # === Makeup / output ===
    C_out:  cap(1u)          # output DC block
    U2:     opamp(tl072)     # makeup amp (inverting, attenuates to ~unity)
    R_o1:   resistor(10k)    # makeup feedback
    R_o2:   resistor(100k)    # makeup input resistor (overall gain trim ~2.2x)
    Output: pot(100k)        # output level
  }
  nets {
    # --- Input buffer ---
    in -> C_in.a
    C_in.b -> R1.a, U0.pos
    R1.b -> gnd
    U0.neg -> U0.out

    # --- Drive amp (inverting, Drive pot in series feedback) ---
    U0.out -> R_in.a
    R_in.b -> U1.neg
    U1.pos -> gnd
    U1.neg -> R_fb.a
    R_fb.b -> Drive.a
    Drive.b -> U1.out

    # --- Drive through the voltage-driven tape head (series colour element) ---
    # Current flows source(R_pri) -> head -> R_sec load to ground. The head
    # develops a saturating voltage drop as it approaches its J-A knee at ~1 V,
    # so the colour node (TH_tape.b) carries the drive minus the nonlinear drop.
    U1.out -> C_drv.a
    C_drv.b -> R_pri.a
    R_pri.b -> TH_tape.a
    TH_tape.b -> R_sec.a, R_bump.a
    R_sec.b -> gnd

    # head-bump LF shelf: R_bump bypassed at LF by C_bump (LF lift)
    R_bump.b -> R_hf.a
    R_bump.a -> C_bump.a
    C_bump.b -> R_bump.b

    # HF rolloff: series R_hf into shunt C_hf + Tone to ground
    R_hf.b -> C_hf.a, Tone.a
    C_hf.b -> gnd
    Tone.b -> gnd

    # --- Makeup amp (inverting) + output level ---
    R_hf.b -> C_out.a
    C_out.b -> R_o2.a
    R_o2.b -> U2.neg
    U2.pos -> gnd
    U2.neg -> R_o1.a
    R_o1.b -> U2.out
    U2.out -> Output.a
    Output.b -> gnd
    Output.w -> out
  }
  controls {
    Drive.position  -> "Drive"  [0.0, 1.0] = 0.35
    Tone.position   -> "Tone"   [0.0, 1.0] = 0.6
    Output.position -> "Output" [0.0, 1.0] = 0.5
  }
}
